IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta97-landholder`

-- Telecommunications Act 1997, Schedule 3 Parts 1 and 3, and s 591 -- worked cases, from the seat of the owner or occupier
-- of land a carrier works on.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2026C00224), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Schedule;
-- the facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Judgments for the carrier or a court are given as facts.
--
-- Clocks: business days for cl 17, 18 and 9, as the person counts them; days for cl 8A and the calendar-year limits.
-- A breached or still-open DEONTIC is asserted through the module's `the rule ends fulfilled` (a CONSIDER on FULFILLED),
-- never with EQUALS.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 17(1), (4). HYPOTHETICAL: Ana owns a farm; a carrier will lay a cable across it (Division 3). 10 business days.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
-- Ana's tenant, Ben, occupies the farm: as an occupier other than the owner he is owed notice too (cl 17(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
-- Cara, a neighbour who neither owns nor occupies the land: cl 17 gives her nothing.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `installing a facility (Division 3)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither the owner nor an occupier, so cl 17 gives me no notice (cl 17(1))`
-- cl 17(4A). A survey of Ana's farm meeting all four conditions: 2 business days. Fail one (a streetscape effect): 10.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 2 business days before the carrier begins this inspection, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(3), (4A))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
-- The 2-day rule is for inspections only (Division 2): installing, with the same four facts, is 10.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
-- cl 17(7). The same low-effect inspection of land that is a public place (a council reserve): no notice at all. Not
-- low-effect, on a public place: 10.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is an inspection of land that is a public place, with none of the listed effects (cl 17(7))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
-- cl 17(5) waiver; (6) urgent work after a storm; waiver is checked first where both hold.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I waived my right to the notice (cl 17(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the work must be done without delay to protect a network or facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property or an adequate level of service (cl 17(6))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I waived my right to the notice (cl 17(5))`
-- cl 17(6A). A temporary defence facility, the carrier considering notice impracticable: none. Not impracticable: 10.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the work concerns a temporary defence facility and the carrier considers notice impracticable (cl 17(6A))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
-- cl 17(8). Installing a temporary emergency-services tower (cl 6(5)(g)): none. Maintenance, same fact: 10 (cl 17(8)
-- speaks only of installing).
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: it is the installation of a temporary low-impact facility for emergency services (cl 17(8), cl 6(5)(g))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: written notice at least 10 business days before the carrier begins, stating its purpose and that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(1)-(4))`
-- Work done under an agreement or a State approval, not under Division 2, 3 or 4: cl 17 does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice before the carrier comes onto my land` `something not done under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: cl 17 applies only to an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 17(2)-(4A). Ana's notice states the purpose and the compensation statement. Work begins on the 10th business day
-- after the notice day: in time. On the 9th: too late.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the notice stated the purpose and the compensation statement and was given early enough (cl 17(2)-(4))`
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE 9 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the notice was given too late (cl 17(4), (4A))`
-- Work begun on the day of the notice itself: too late.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the notice was given too late (cl 17(4), (4A))`
-- A low-effect survey: the 2nd business day is in time, the 1st is not. Not low-effect: the 2nd is too late.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE TRUE 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the notice stated the purpose and the compensation statement and was given early enough (cl 17(2)-(4))`
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE TRUE 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the notice was given too late (cl 17(4), (4A))`
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE TRUE 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the notice was given too late (cl 17(4), (4A))`
-- No purpose stated; no compensation statement (each defeats a notice given in good time); work outside Divisions 2-4.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` FALSE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the notice did not specify the purpose of the activity (cl 17(2))`
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE FALSE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the notice did not state that compensation may be payable under clause 42 (cl 17(3))`
#ASSERT `Was the notice I was given good enough` `something not done under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3` TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: cl 17 applies only to an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3`
-- The same as a prohibition, clock from the notice day: beginning on business day 10 is fulfilled, on day 9 a breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`cl 17(4), (4A) -- the carrier must not begin before the notice period has run` 10) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin the activity on my land` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`cl 17(4), (4A) -- the carrier must not begin before the notice period has run` 10) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin the activity on my land` 9))))
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`cl 17(4), (4A) -- the carrier must not begin before the notice period has run` 2) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin the activity on my land` 2)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`cl 17(4), (4A) -- the carrier must not begin before the notice period has run` 2) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin the activity on my land` 1))))
-- expect: BREACH BY the carrier, "cl 17(4), (4A): ..."
#TRACE `cl 17(4), (4A) -- the carrier must not begin before the notice period has run` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the carrier` DOES `begin the activity on my land` AT 9

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 18. HYPOTHETICAL: the carrier wants a windbreak on Ana's farm lopped for its cable. It asked her in writing 10
-- business days ahead; she did not do it in the period: the carrier may. She did: it may not.
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 FALSE EQUALS `yes: I did not do the work the carrier's request asked for within the period it specified, so the carrier may do it itself (cl 18(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 TRUE EQUALS `no: I did what the carrier's request asked within the period it specified, so the carrier may not do it itself (cl 18(2))`
-- Asked only 9 business days ahead; never asked.
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 9 FALSE EQUALS `no: the carrier's request was not given at least 10 business days before the work (cl 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: the carrier must first give me a written request, at least 10 business days before, asking me to do it myself in a stated manner and period (cl 18(1), (2))`
-- Ben, the tenant, is owed the request as occupier.
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 12 FALSE EQUALS `yes: I did not do the work the carrier's request asked for within the period it specified, so the carrier may do it itself (cl 18(2))`
-- Waiver (cl 18(3)), urgent work (18(4)), a temporary defence facility the carrier finds impracticable (18(3A)), and
-- the same facility where it does not.
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `cl 18 does not stand in the way: I waived my right to the request (cl 18(3))`
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `cl 18 does not stand in the way: the work must be done without delay to protect a network or facility, people's health or safety, the environment, property or an adequate level of service (cl 18(4))`
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `cl 18 does not stand in the way: the work concerns a temporary defence facility and the carrier considers the request impracticable (cl 18(3A))`
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: the carrier must first give me a written request, at least 10 business days before, asking me to do it myself in a stated manner and period (cl 18(1), (2))`
-- Trees on public land, or outside Division 2-4 work, or for someone neither owner nor occupier: cl 18 does not reach.
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: cl 18 applies only to trees, undergrowth or vegetation on private land, cut or cleared in an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4, and gives the request only to the owner and an occupier`
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `something not done under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: cl 18 applies only to trees, undergrowth or vegetation on private land, cut or cleared in an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4, and gives the request only to the owner and an occupier`
#ASSERT `Can the carrier cut my trees or clear my vegetation` `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: cl 18 applies only to trees, undergrowth or vegetation on private land, cut or cleared in an activity under Division 2, 3 or 4, and gives the request only to the owner and an occupier`
-- As a rule over time, the request giving Ana 15 business days: she lops on day 15, done. The period passes and the
-- carrier lops on day 17: done. The carrier lops on day 3, while her period runs: not fulfilled (its act does not count).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`cl 18(1), (2) -- I am asked to do it myself; only if I do not may the carrier` 15) 0 (LIST (EVENT `me, the landholder` `cut down, lop or clear as the carrier requested` 15)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`cl 18(1), (2) -- I am asked to do it myself; only if I do not may the carrier` 15) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 16), (EVENT `the carrier` `cut down, lop or clear the trees or vegetation itself` 17)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`cl 18(1), (2) -- I am asked to do it myself; only if I do not may the carrier` 15) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `cut down, lop or clear the trees or vegetation itself` 3))))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 8A. Each kind of temporary facility and its 28-day clock; the holiday tower has none.
#ASSERT `By when must the temporary facility be removed` `a temporary tower while another facility is maintained (cl 6(5)(b))` EQUALS `within 28 days after the maintenance of the other facility is completed (cl 8A(1))`
#ASSERT `By when must the temporary facility be removed` `a temporary tower while another facility is replaced (cl 6(5)(c))` EQUALS `within 28 days after the replacement of the other facility is completed (cl 8A(2))`
#ASSERT `By when must the temporary facility be removed` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` EQUALS `within 28 days after the end of the event (cl 8A(3))`
#ASSERT `By when must the temporary facility be removed` `a temporary tower for a series of events at a venue (cl 6(5)(e))` EQUALS `within 28 days after the end of the last of the events (cl 8A(4))`
#ASSERT `By when must the temporary facility be removed` `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))` EQUALS `cl 8A sets no removal deadline for a holiday-period tower; it may stay at the place no more than 90 days in a calendar year (cl 8C)`
#ASSERT `By when must the temporary facility be removed` `a temporary tower for emergency services in an emergency or natural disaster (cl 6(5)(g))` EQUALS `within 28 days after it ceases to be needed for emergency services to deal with the emergency or natural disaster (cl 8A(5))`
#ASSERT `By when must the temporary facility be removed` `a temporary facility while the original facility is maintained (cl 7(3A))` EQUALS `within 28 days after the maintenance of the original facility is completed (cl 8A(6))`
-- HYPOTHETICAL: a festival tower on Dev's paddock; the festival ends on day 0. Removed on day 28: done. Day 29: breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `cl 8A -- the carrier must remove the temporary facility within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `remove the temporary facility` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE `cl 8A -- the carrier must remove the temporary facility within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `remove the temporary facility` 29))))
-- expect: BREACH BY the carrier, "cl 8A: ..."
#TRACE `cl 8A -- the carrier must remove the temporary facility within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
-- The same, as the seat question that runs the rule. Dev's festival tower: removed on day 28, in time; day 29, late.
-- Not removed, day 20 or day 28: not yet late; not removed by day 29: late. A maintenance tower removed on day 5: in time.
-- A holiday tower: cl 8A has no deadline.
#ASSERT `Was the temporary facility removed in time` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` TRUE 28 EQUALS `in time: the carrier removed the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
#ASSERT `Was the temporary facility removed in time` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` TRUE 29 EQUALS `late: the carrier did not remove the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
#ASSERT `Was the temporary facility removed in time` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` FALSE 20 EQUALS `not yet late: the 28 days have not run out (cl 8A)`
#ASSERT `Was the temporary facility removed in time` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` FALSE 28 EQUALS `not yet late: the 28 days have not run out (cl 8A)`
#ASSERT `Was the temporary facility removed in time` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` FALSE 29 EQUALS `late: the carrier did not remove the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
#ASSERT `Was the temporary facility removed in time` `a temporary facility while the original facility is maintained (cl 7(3A))` TRUE 5 EQUALS `in time: the carrier removed the temporary facility within 28 days (cl 8A)`
#ASSERT `Was the temporary facility removed in time` `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))` TRUE 100 EQUALS `not covered: cl 8A sets no removal deadline for a holiday-period tower; see the calendar-year limit in cl 8C`
-- cl 8B: event towers, 183 days a calendar year is allowed, 184 is not. cl 8C: holiday towers, 90 and 91.
#ASSERT `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` 183 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` `a temporary tower for an event at a venue (cl 6(5)(d))` 184 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` `a temporary tower for a series of events at a venue (cl 6(5)(e))` 184 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))` 90 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` `a temporary tower for a high-demand holiday period (cl 6(5)(f))` 91 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No calendar-year limit for maintenance, replacement or emergency towers (their limit is the 28-day removal).
#ASSERT `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` `a temporary tower while another facility is maintained (cl 6(5)(b))` 400 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Have temporary towers stayed beyond the calendar-year limit` `a temporary tower for emergency services in an emergency or natural disaster (cl 6(5)(g))` 200 EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 9, 9A. No agreement: 10 business days. Ana agreed 20, nobody else occupies: 20. Ben occupies and did not agree: 10.
-- Both agreed: 20. An "agreed" 10 is no later start; 11 is.
#ASSERT `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` TRUE FALSE FALSE 20 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` TRUE TRUE FALSE 20 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` TRUE TRUE TRUE 20 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` TRUE FALSE FALSE 10 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` TRUE FALSE FALSE 11 EQUALS 11
-- Only the occupier agreeing is not enough (cl 9(3)(a) needs the owner).
#ASSERT `How many business days does the carrier have to begin restoring my land` FALSE TRUE TRUE 30 EQUALS 10
-- As a rule: begun on business day 10, done; nothing by day 11, breach; an agreed 20, begun on day 20, done.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4) -- the carrier must begin restoring my land in time` 10) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin restoring my land` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE (`cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4) -- the carrier must begin restoring my land in time` 10) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 11))))
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4) -- the carrier must begin restoring my land in time` 20) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the carrier` `begin restoring my land` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- The seat question that runs the rule. No agreement: begun on business day 10, in time; on day 11, late. Not begun, 7
-- or 10 business days on: not yet late; 11 on: late. Ana agreed 20 and no one else occupies: begun on day 18, in time.
-- Ben occupies and did not agree, so the period stays 10: begun on day 18, late.
#ASSERT `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 10 EQUALS `in time: the carrier began restoring my land within the period (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 11 EQUALS `late: the carrier did not begin restoring my land within the period, so it must show it took all reasonable steps to ensure that it did (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 7 EQUALS `not yet late: the period for beginning restoration has not run out (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 10 EQUALS `not yet late: the period for beginning restoration has not run out (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 11 EQUALS `late: the carrier did not begin restoring my land within the period, so it must show it took all reasonable steps to ensure that it did (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` TRUE FALSE FALSE 20 TRUE 18 EQUALS `in time: the carrier began restoring my land within the period (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Did the carrier begin restoring my land in time` TRUE TRUE FALSE 20 TRUE 18 EQUALS `late: the carrier did not begin restoring my land within the period, so it must show it took all reasonable steps to ensure that it did (cl 9(2), 9A(3), (4))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 42. Ana: the contractor's trench killed a crop on land she owns: yes. Ben, the tenant, loses his own stock feed: yes
-- (an interest). A survey that damages her bore: yes. No loss; work outside Division 2-4; not caused by the carrier or its
-- people; property that is neither hers nor one she has an interest in.
#ASSERT `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` TRUE `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, as agreed between us or, failing agreement, as a court decides; it covers temporary as well as permanent damage and the taking of sand, soil, stone, gravel, timber, water and other things, and no ACMA limit on tort damages applies to it (cl 42(1), (2), 46(7))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` TRUE `maintaining a facility (Division 4)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, as agreed between us or, failing agreement, as a court decides; it covers temporary as well as permanent damage and the taking of sand, soil, stone, gravel, timber, water and other things, and no ACMA limit on tort damages applies to it (cl 42(1), (2), 46(7))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` TRUE `inspecting or surveying my land (Division 2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, as agreed between us or, failing agreement, as a court decides; it covers temporary as well as permanent damage and the taking of sand, soil, stone, gravel, timber, water and other things, and no ACMA limit on tort damages applies to it (cl 42(1), (2), 46(7))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` FALSE `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no compensation under cl 42: I have not suffered financial loss or damage (cl 42(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` TRUE `something not done under Division 2, 3 or 4 of Schedule 3` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no compensation under cl 42: the loss or damage was not caused by anything the carrier, its employees or contractors did under Division 2, 3 or 4 (cl 42(1), 43)`
#ASSERT `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` TRUE `installing a facility (Division 3)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no compensation under cl 42: the loss or damage was not caused by anything the carrier, its employees or contractors did under Division 2, 3 or 4 (cl 42(1), 43)`
#ASSERT `Can I claim compensation for loss or damage from the carrier` TRUE `installing a facility (Division 3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no compensation under cl 42: the loss or damage is not in relation to property I own or have an interest in (cl 42(1)(a), (b))`
-- cl 42(3). Claim $50,000, local court limit $100,000: any of them. Claim equal to the limit: still ("not less than").
-- One dollar over: Federal or Supreme Court only. No local court: the same.
#ASSERT `Which courts can decide my compensation` 50000 100000 EQUALS `the Federal Court, the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is, or a local inferior court whose debt limit is at least my claim (cl 42(3))`
#ASSERT `Which courts can decide my compensation` 100000 100000 EQUALS `the Federal Court, the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is, or a local inferior court whose debt limit is at least my claim (cl 42(3))`
#ASSERT `Which courts can decide my compensation` 100001 100000 EQUALS `the Federal Court or the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is; my claim is above the local inferior court's debt limit (cl 42(3))`
#ASSERT `Which courts can decide my compensation` 5000 0 EQUALS `the Federal Court or the Supreme Court of the State or Territory where the property is; my claim is above the local inferior court's debt limit (cl 42(3))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 62, 63; s 591. A carrier's facility under Schedule 3 is found to acquire property from Ana, after the 2005
-- amendments: the carrier pays. Before them, or from another part of the Act: the Commonwealth (s 591). No acquisition,
-- or one valid without compensation: neither.
#ASSERT `Who must compensate me for an acquisition of my property` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the carrier must pay me a reasonable amount of compensation, agreed or, failing agreement, decided by a court; anything I already obtained or recovered for the same event is taken into account, and my cl 42 claim is not limited (cl 62)`
#ASSERT `Who must compensate me for an acquisition of my property` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commonwealth is liable to pay me a reasonable amount of compensation; failing agreement I may sue it in the Federal Court (s 591)`
#ASSERT `Who must compensate me for an acquisition of my property` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Commonwealth is liable to pay me a reasonable amount of compensation; failing agreement I may sue it in the Federal Court (s 591)`
#ASSERT `Who must compensate me for an acquisition of my property` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no compensation under cl 62 or s 591: there is no acquisition of my property that would be invalid without compensation (cl 62(1), s 591(1))`
#ASSERT `Who must compensate me for an acquisition of my property` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no compensation under cl 62 or s 591: there is no acquisition of my property that would be invalid without compensation (cl 62(1), s 591(1))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- cl 47. The carrier's pit set in concrete on Ana's farm stays the carrier's, fixture or not; unless the circumstances
-- indicate otherwise.
#ASSERT `Is the carrier's facility on my land mine` FALSE EQUALS `not mine: the facility remains the property of its owner even if it has become a fixture on my land (cl 47(a))`
#ASSERT `Is the carrier's facility on my land mine` TRUE EQUALS `cl 47 does not settle it: the circumstances indicate otherwise, so ownership turns on those circumstances (cl 47)`
-- cl 53. HYPOTHETICAL: Ana subdivides; the carrier, of opinion that the pit must move, reasonably spends on moving it: she
-- pays the reasonable part. Ben, who did not subdivide: no. No such opinion; no costs: no.
#ASSERT `Must I pay for moving the facility because I subdivided` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I must pay the carrier so much of its costs as is reasonable, and it may recover that amount from me in court as a debt (cl 53)`
#ASSERT `Must I pay for moving the facility because I subdivided` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: cl 53 makes only the person who subdivided the land liable`
#ASSERT `Must I pay for moving the facility because I subdivided` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the carrier is not of the opinion that the subdivision made the removal or alteration necessary (cl 53(a))`
#ASSERT `Must I pay for moving the facility because I subdivided` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the carrier has incurred no costs in anything reasonably done for the removal or alteration (cl 53(b))`
